---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Rust Cheat Sheet | Free Ownership, Borrowing & Syntax Reference"
  description="Complete Rust cheat sheet with ownership, borrowing, lifetimes, traits, and common patterns. Free reference for Rust developers."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Rust<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Ownership, borrowing, lifetimes, traits, and common patterns. From basics to advanced Rust.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Variables & Mutability</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Basic Types</h3>
        <pre><code>let x: i32 = 42;
let y: f64 = 3.14;
let s: &str = "hello";
let b: bool = true;
let c: char = 'A';</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Mutability</h3>
        <pre><code>let x = 5;          // immutable
let mut y = 5;      // mutable
y = 10;             // OK

let x = "shadowed"; // shadowing
let x: i32 = 42;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Ownership & Borrowing</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Ownership Rules</h3>
        <pre><code>// Each value has one owner
let s1 = String::from("hello");
let s2 = s1;           // s1 moved to s2
// println!("{}", s1); // ERROR: s1 is gone

// Clone for deep copy
let s3 = s2.clone();</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Borrowing</h3>
        <pre><code>// Immutable borrow
fn greet(name: &amp;str) {
    println!("Hello, {name}");
}

// Mutable borrow
fn push(s: &amp;mut String) {
    s.push_str(" world");
}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Structs & Enums</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Structs</h3>
        <pre><code>struct User {
    name: String,
    age: u32,
}

let user = User {
    name: String::from("Alice"),
    age: 30,
};</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Enums &amp; Pattern Matching</h3>
        <pre><code>enum Shape {
    Circle(f64),
    Square(f64),
}

match shape {
    Shape::Circle(r) => pi * r * r,
    Shape::Square(s) => s * s,
}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Error Handling</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Option &amp; Result</h3>
        <pre><code>// Option: value or nothing
let maybe: Option&lt;i32&gt; = Some(42);
let none: Option&lt;i32&gt; = None;

// Result: success or error
let res: Result&lt;i32, Error&gt;
    = Ok(42);</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Unwrapping</h3>
        <pre><code>let val = maybe.unwrap();
let val = maybe.unwrap_or(0);
let val = maybe.unwrap_or_else(|| {
    expensive_default()
});</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Common Traits</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Trait Definitions</h3>
        <pre><code>trait Summary {
    fn summarize(&amp;self) -> String;
}

impl Summary for Article {
    fn summarize(&amp;self) -> String {
        format!("{}...", &amp;self.title)
    }
}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
